{
  "slug": "context-bench",
  "name": "Context Bench",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Plugin description:\nSelf-learning Claude Code plugin that\nautomatically detects what project you're\nworking on and injects the right file context\ninto every session. No manual configuration\nneeded — it learns from your usage patterns,\nbuilds confidence scores, and removes stale\ntopics automatically. Uses three hooks:\nUserPromptSubmit (match & inject), PostToolUse\n(track changes), SessionEnd (learn & decay).\nZero dependencies, Python 3.9+ stdlib only.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Hooks** (3): `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolUse`, `SessionEnd`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install context-bench@claude-community` from `nessos666/context-bench`.\n\nEvery Claude Code session starts the same way: you tell it what project you're working on, what files matter, what the architecture looks like. Then the next session, you do it again.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "hook",
